  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Suppose the mass of a single Ag-atom is $m$. Ag metal crystallises in fcc lattice with unit cell of length $a$. The density of Ag metal in terms of $a$ and $m$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Om6Ji",
      "text": "$\\frac{4 m}{a^{3}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kmXt4",
      "text": "$\\frac{2 m}{a^{3}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cR2Je",
      "text": "$\\frac{m}{a^{3}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "BGj9H",
      "text": "$\\frac{m}{4 a^{3}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given that,\r\nMass of single Ag-atom $=m$\r\nUnit cell length $=a$\r\nTotal atoms present per unit cell of fcc lattice $=4$ \r\nTherefore, mass of unit cell becomes $4 \\mathrm{m}$. \r\nVolume of unit cell $=a^{3}$\r\nDensity $(\\rho)=\\frac{\\text { Mass of unit cell }}{\\text { Volume of unit cell }}=\\frac{4 \\mathrm{m}}{\\mathrm{a}^{3}}$",
    "image": null
  },
